WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:04.169
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.236 --> 00:07.555
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.623 --> 00:11.009
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.093 --> 00:13.978
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.063 --> 00:17.599
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.650 --> 00:20.818
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.886 --> 00:22.420
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.488 --> 00:23.838
♪ Laugh and cry

00:23.906 --> 00:27.797
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.453 --> 00:37.536
Good evening. I'm Tom
Tucker bringing you news

00:37.537 --> 00:39.237
you heard four hours
ago on the Internet.

00:39.305 --> 00:41.506
Our top story: A mishap
in Quahog harbor today.

00:41.574 --> 00:43.008
That's right, Tom.

00:43.075 --> 00:44.442
A ferry carrying a shipment

00:44.510 --> 00:47.379
of brand-new Mercedes
Benzes from Germany

00:47.446 --> 00:49.614
crashed and sank just
a few miles off our coast.

00:49.682 --> 00:52.184
Thus far, the cars
remain on the ocean floor

00:52.251 --> 00:54.553
as the Germans refuse
to clean up the disaster.

00:54.620 --> 00:56.221
The German
Environmental Minister

00:56.289 --> 00:57.822
called a press
conference to issue

00:57.890 --> 00:59.224
the following statement:

00:59.292 --> 01:02.077
(thick German accent):
I see nothing! I know nothing!

01:02.144 --> 01:03.679
Holy crap! Did you
hear that, Lois?

01:03.680 --> 01:05.849
All them fancy cars out
there in the ocean, just

01:05.874 --> 01:06.798
free for the taking?

01:06.799 --> 01:08.200
I'm gonna get me a Mercedes!

01:08.267 --> 01:10.719
Peter, that may be the
stupidest idea you've ever had.

01:10.786 --> 01:13.088
And you've had some
pretty stupid ones.

01:13.155 --> 01:14.822
Hi there. Peter Griffin.

01:14.874 --> 01:17.542
<i>You know, a lot of us here
at Family Guy are, frankly,</i>

01:17.627 --> 01:19.994
sickened by the sorry state
of education in this country

01:20.046 --> 01:22.013
and how little
you people read anymore.

01:22.098 --> 01:24.883
So, for this next cutaway,
we're gonna make you read it.

01:24.967 --> 01:26.334
That's right, you heard me.

01:26.385 --> 01:28.303
Do a little work
once in a while,

01:28.354 --> 01:29.554
instead of having
everything spoon-fed.

01:29.639 --> 01:31.691
You want your yuks,
put in a little effort.

01:31.775 --> 01:32.808
All right, go ahead.

01:51.712 --> 01:53.713
Okay, that one might
have been more of a visual,

01:53.797 --> 01:55.581
but you feel that feeling
you got right now?

01:55.666 --> 01:58.467
That's satisfaction.
You just read something.

01:58.535 --> 02:00.869
And no one can take
that away from you.

02:00.921 --> 02:02.171
Proud of you.

02:09.379 --> 02:11.547
Geez, you're a mess.
What is that?

02:11.598 --> 02:13.449
It was finger-paint day.
What the hell?

02:13.517 --> 02:15.451
Why didn't they clean
you up before you left?

02:15.519 --> 02:17.553
Brian, there's, like,
37 other kids in there.

02:17.604 --> 02:20.323
One was in a drawer all day.
Wow, seems like Lois would've

02:20.390 --> 02:22.325
checked that stuff out
before sending you.

02:22.392 --> 02:23.659
Yeah, you'd think so, right?

02:23.727 --> 02:25.411
I mean, it's clearly
not a place of business.

02:25.495 --> 02:26.946
It's someone's house.

02:27.014 --> 02:29.215
You know, half the time you
can hear someone showering.

02:29.283 --> 02:32.067
I mean, you never see them, but
you can hear the shower going.

02:32.119 --> 02:34.003
Really? That seems weird.
Yeah, and is it normal

02:34.070 --> 02:36.005
that Miss Emily tied
us all to the sink

02:36.072 --> 02:38.257
while she went out to
return a birthday present?

02:38.342 --> 02:39.675
No, that's not
normal at all.

02:39.743 --> 02:41.010
You know, Stewie,
maybe I should

02:41.077 --> 02:42.578
come by tomorrow
and check things out.

02:42.629 --> 02:44.347
That teacher sounds
really irresponsible.

02:44.414 --> 02:46.098
She is. Adults are stupid.

02:46.183 --> 02:49.268
The world would be so much
better if it were run by babies.

02:49.353 --> 02:51.354
<i>TV ANNOUNCER:
Tonight on NBC... Shapes!</i>

02:51.421 --> 02:52.855
(excited cooing)

02:52.922 --> 02:54.640
<i>And then... Colors!</i>

02:54.725 --> 02:56.025
(excited cooing)

02:56.092 --> 02:58.260
<i>Followed by
an all-new... Dad's Keys!</i>

02:58.312 --> 03:00.146
(cheering, cooing)

03:01.698 --> 03:03.399
(quiet snoring)

03:08.055 --> 03:09.640
Man, I can't wait
to get a Mercedes.

03:09.641 --> 03:10.258
Me, either.

03:10.259 --> 03:12.160
Yeah, it's gonna be sweet.

03:14.478 --> 03:16.012
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa!

03:16.079 --> 03:18.247
What the hell is that?!
A sun hat.

03:18.315 --> 03:20.666
No, no, no, no, no.
What do you mean, no?

03:20.751 --> 03:22.551
I'm protecting my face
and neck from the sun.

03:22.619 --> 03:23.753
Use sunscreen!
Y-You don't need

03:23.820 --> 03:25.388
to put a circus
on your head.

03:25.455 --> 03:26.922
This is a ploy
for attention.

03:26.990 --> 03:28.190
Sunscreens are
bad for you.

03:28.258 --> 03:29.592
The chemicals get
in your skin.

03:29.659 --> 03:31.410
Boy, you really want
to wear that hat.

03:31.478 --> 03:33.546
That hat's coming off!
No!

03:33.613 --> 03:35.564
(grunting)

03:38.585 --> 03:39.819
You guys are jerks!

03:39.886 --> 03:41.987
I can have my own identity
besides you two.

03:42.055 --> 03:44.173
Not this way.
Not the hat way.

03:45.475 --> 03:48.060
Holy crap!
I think we got one!

03:50.163 --> 03:52.031
Aw, damn it!
It's just a dolphin.

03:52.115 --> 03:53.082
(with British accent):
Sorry,

03:53.149 --> 03:54.450
did I get in the way
of something?

03:54.501 --> 03:55.868
No, it's all right.
We were just trying

03:55.952 --> 03:57.370
to get some of them
sunken Mercedes.

03:57.454 --> 03:59.872
Oh, yeah, there's a great big
pile of them down there.

03:59.956 --> 04:02.124
Me and my mates, right,
we was having a laugh

04:02.175 --> 04:04.326
sitting in of one of them,
pretending to be people.

04:04.378 --> 04:06.011
(chuckles)
You know, like, driving around

04:06.096 --> 04:07.963
getting into incidents
with other motorists.

04:08.014 --> 04:10.349
Honk, honk. "Stay out
the way, you old bat!"

04:10.434 --> 04:11.600
Asian.

04:11.668 --> 04:14.019
Not all Asians
are bad drivers.

04:14.087 --> 04:16.171
No, no, not
all terrorists are Arab.

04:16.223 --> 04:19.275
<i>But, you know, they are, so...</i>

04:19.342 --> 04:20.693
Uh, well, I'm Peter,

04:20.761 --> 04:22.762
and that's, uh, Joe,
and that's Quagmire.

04:22.829 --> 04:24.046
Name's Billy, Billy Finn.

04:24.114 --> 04:25.531
It's got "fin" in it.

04:25.615 --> 04:26.899
I didn't pick it.

04:26.983 --> 04:28.350
(chuckles):
Luck of the draw.

04:28.402 --> 04:31.405
Say, you want me to try
and get you one of those cars

04:31.489 --> 04:32.689
from down there, yeah?

04:32.757 --> 04:34.724
(gasps)
You would do that?!

04:34.726 --> 04:35.892
Well, I could try.

04:35.960 --> 04:38.395
Here, let me
give it a go.

04:38.463 --> 04:39.513
He seems nice.

04:39.580 --> 04:40.964
He does.
Yeah.

04:42.467 --> 04:45.235
So, uh, what do you have
planned for the summer?

04:45.303 --> 04:48.638
I'm sure he'll
be right back.

04:48.706 --> 04:51.675
Sorry, mate, all I could get
was this hood ornament.

04:51.726 --> 04:53.210
(gasps)
This is just as good!

04:53.277 --> 04:55.212
Thank you so much!
Hey, you know,

04:55.279 --> 04:57.481
if there's ever anything
I could do for you...

04:57.548 --> 04:58.982
Actually, you could
do something.

04:59.050 --> 05:00.934
You could eat only
dolphin-safe tuna.

05:01.018 --> 05:03.520
Wait, is that the brand
that costs five cents more?

05:03.571 --> 05:04.888
No, I can't do that.

05:04.939 --> 05:07.073
Things ain't so good
in America right now,

05:07.158 --> 05:08.992
which is why
we're all so fat.

05:13.230 --> 05:14.714
What did I tell you, Brian?

05:14.782 --> 05:16.049
It's a nightmare in here.

05:16.117 --> 05:17.551
Oh, my God!

05:27.044 --> 05:29.429
Oh, what happened to that kid?
He fell off a stool

05:29.497 --> 05:30.864
trying to turn off
Maury Povich.

05:30.932 --> 05:32.482
This is awful!
Where's your teacher?

05:32.550 --> 05:34.468
Probably out back.

05:36.587 --> 05:38.321
Excuse me, are you Miss Emily?

05:38.389 --> 05:40.323
Yeah. Hi. Who are you?

05:40.391 --> 05:41.825
Uh, Brian.

05:41.893 --> 05:43.593
Brian Steel.

05:43.661 --> 05:45.462
I was just
dropping Stewie off.

05:45.530 --> 05:47.914
Oh, yeah! I should
probably go back in there,

05:47.982 --> 05:49.316
see how everyone's
doing, I guess.

05:49.383 --> 05:50.417
Ah, they're fine.

05:50.485 --> 05:52.819
In fact, I see Stewie
reading a book.

05:52.887 --> 05:56.256
<i>Scratch-and-sniff
Lindsay Lohan Goes Jogging.</i>

05:58.626 --> 06:00.377
Oh, God! That's terrible!

06:00.444 --> 06:01.912
Oh, here's a pop-up book.

06:01.979 --> 06:04.047
<i>Tommy Lee Goes Boating.</i>

06:08.352 --> 06:10.287
Move, Lois! You're on
the hood ornament's pillow.

06:10.354 --> 06:12.105
Peter, put that away.
It's time for bed.

06:12.173 --> 06:14.107
W-Wait, hang on, Lois,
before I go to bed,

06:14.175 --> 06:15.559
I just got
to do one thing.

06:18.162 --> 06:18.716
Hello?

06:18.741 --> 06:20.711
Hey, Mr. Pewterschmidt,
it's me, Peter.

06:20.898 --> 06:23.466
You remember how you said
I'd never amount to nothing?

06:24.669 --> 06:26.036
Is that a Mercedes?

06:26.103 --> 06:27.704
Peter, hang up the phone.
(doorbell rings)

06:27.772 --> 06:29.990
My God, who could be at
the door at this hour?

06:30.057 --> 06:32.859
I don't know, but this late,
it's got to be bad news.

06:32.927 --> 06:34.694
Everyone knows you
always get bad news

06:34.762 --> 06:35.929
in the middle of the night.

06:38.199 --> 06:40.350
Wake up, wake up, wake up!
Huh? What?

06:40.418 --> 06:41.685
You have cancer!
What?!

06:41.752 --> 06:43.119
Yeah. I thought
you should know.

06:43.187 --> 06:44.955
Okay, go back to sleep.

06:45.022 --> 06:46.356
Wait, I have questions.

06:46.424 --> 06:49.092
<i>(sighs)
It's very late.</i>

06:50.378 --> 06:52.329
<i>Oh, hello. This
is the right house.</i>

06:52.396 --> 06:53.563
(chuckles)
That's good, then.

06:53.631 --> 06:54.864
What the hell?

06:54.932 --> 06:56.700
It's me, Billy. Billy Finn.

06:56.767 --> 06:59.736
Just wanted to take you up
on your nice offer from earlier.

06:59.804 --> 07:02.072
What... I-I don't... What offer?

07:02.139 --> 07:03.623
(snickers)
You know, the bit about

07:03.691 --> 07:05.792
"If there's ever
anything I can do,"

07:05.860 --> 07:08.495
so, yeah...
Oh.

07:08.563 --> 07:11.231
Yeah, thought I might
make a go of it on land.

07:11.299 --> 07:13.166
So, "anything you
can ever do."

07:13.234 --> 07:15.535
Here I am. Thank you.

07:15.603 --> 07:17.370
Squid pro quo.
(chuckles)

07:17.438 --> 07:19.773
Thank you for not
being "shellfish."

07:19.840 --> 07:21.942
(giggles) I just said that
for the "halibut."

07:22.009 --> 07:25.078
(laughs)
Fish puns.

07:25.146 --> 07:26.680
Ah. Oh, cod.

07:26.747 --> 07:28.648
(laughing)

07:28.716 --> 07:30.350
Oh, God, come on.

07:30.418 --> 07:32.019
(grunts)
Let me in.

07:32.087 --> 07:33.888
Peter, who is it?
Is Meg dead?

07:33.956 --> 07:36.290
It's that dolphin--
I think he wants to crash here.

07:36.358 --> 07:38.092
And I have no info on Meg.

07:38.160 --> 07:39.260
He wants to what?

07:39.328 --> 07:40.561
I-I'm not sure that...

07:40.629 --> 07:41.896
I brought a gift.

07:41.980 --> 07:44.632
Put it to your ear.
You can hear the ocean.

07:44.700 --> 07:46.267
♪ Caribbean Queen

07:46.335 --> 07:48.736
♪ Now we're sharing...
It's broken or something.

07:48.804 --> 07:50.771
<i>All I hear is...
It's Billy Ocean!</i>

07:50.839 --> 07:52.840
(cackling)

07:52.908 --> 07:54.809
Oh, God! I got
loads more.

08:05.484 --> 08:08.553
So, Billy, I, uh, I hope
the couch was all right?

08:08.558 --> 08:09.959
Yeah, a lot better
than the floor.

08:10.026 --> 08:12.528
And I should know, 'cause
I went down on the floor,

08:12.596 --> 08:14.751
thinking it had to be a
lot better than the couch.

08:14.752 --> 08:17.087
Okay, well,
breakfast is ready.

08:17.154 --> 08:18.355
Oh. Uh...

08:18.422 --> 08:20.323
Is everything all right?

08:20.391 --> 08:22.859
Yeah. Well, it's just...

08:22.927 --> 08:24.393
would you mind tossing
it up in the air for me?

08:24.418 --> 08:25.818
Well, I don't know...

08:26.063 --> 08:27.464
Lois, he is our guest.

08:27.531 --> 08:29.265
Toss it in the air.

08:32.453 --> 08:36.139
Uh, I'm used to a
little applause, so...

08:36.207 --> 08:38.191
(faint clapping)

08:38.242 --> 08:39.209
All right, all right.

08:39.276 --> 08:40.710
Not bad. Afternoon crowd.

08:40.778 --> 08:42.946
Lightly attended.

08:43.014 --> 08:44.981
So, Billy, how long will
you be staying with us?

08:45.049 --> 08:46.616
Are you kidding?
As long as he wants!

08:46.684 --> 08:49.019
Yay! We live with a dolphin!

08:50.788 --> 08:53.556
Anyway, I'm off
to read Meg's diary.

08:53.624 --> 08:55.274
Only been here one night,
but I get the sense

08:55.299 --> 08:56.984
we all dislike Meg.

08:57.111 --> 09:00.780
Um, I'm a dolphin--
smart, intuitive.

09:00.848 --> 09:04.401
Also, Peter told me
in the hall. Ha.

09:04.468 --> 09:07.120
Peter, I'm not so sure about
Billy staying here with us.

09:07.188 --> 09:08.700
What are you talking about?
He's hilarious.

09:08.725 --> 09:09.439
I don't know.

09:09.440 --> 09:11.775
Listen, just leave it to me.
I'm great with animals.

09:11.842 --> 09:13.359
Remember when I lived
with those ants?

09:14.812 --> 09:17.230
We're working on something.

09:22.236 --> 09:24.904
Yes? May I help you?

09:24.972 --> 09:26.305
Hey, put him down!

09:26.357 --> 09:28.191
Who are you?
I-I can't stop him!

09:28.275 --> 09:29.409
Can anyone stop him?

09:29.477 --> 09:31.244
No? Well, he's gone.

09:31.312 --> 09:33.113
Hey, Stewie.
How's it going?

09:33.164 --> 09:36.066
Brian, what are you doing here?
Came by to check on my pal.

09:36.133 --> 09:38.134
Where's, uh, Miss Emily?
I haven't seen her yet today.

09:38.202 --> 09:40.637
She gave me the keys to open
up when she left yesterday.

09:40.704 --> 09:42.639
I thought you said you
were gonna talk to her.

09:42.706 --> 09:44.674
I did, a-and she's doing
her best, you know?

09:44.742 --> 09:46.409
She's got a lot
on her plate.

09:46.477 --> 09:48.044
She's got school.
She's got work.

09:48.112 --> 09:49.312
This is her work!

09:49.380 --> 09:50.647
Oh, hi, Brian.

09:50.714 --> 09:53.283
I thought you had a busy day
at your legal practice.

09:53.350 --> 09:54.918
(groans) Oh...

09:54.985 --> 09:57.153
Hey, Emily! Yeah, I had
some time between cases.

09:57.221 --> 09:59.055
I thought I'd see
how you were doing.

09:59.123 --> 10:00.590
That's so nice of you!

10:00.658 --> 10:02.525
Let me just put
these bags away

10:02.593 --> 10:05.895
and throw some saltines
in the yard for the kids.

10:05.963 --> 10:07.416
You're disgusting.

10:07.441 --> 10:08.797
Hey, I'm sorry,
but Miss Emily and I

10:08.799 --> 10:11.134
have a connection, which
is totally unexpected.

10:11.202 --> 10:13.476
And by the way,
I actually think she's

10:13.501 --> 10:14.437
doing a pretty good job.

10:14.438 --> 10:15.839
She's teaching you
guys independence.

10:15.906 --> 10:17.273
We're one!

10:17.341 --> 10:19.275
Independence means we die!

10:19.343 --> 10:21.227
Do you like this?
I just got it.

10:21.295 --> 10:23.196
Say you like it, or
she's gonna spend

10:23.264 --> 10:25.265
the rest of the afternoon
out returning that stuff.

10:25.332 --> 10:26.983
Looks great!

10:27.051 --> 10:28.968
Wow, you really
fill these things up.

10:29.036 --> 10:31.605
Hey, do you think maybe you'd
want to hang out sometime?

10:31.673 --> 10:33.474
What, you mean like
a movie or something?

10:33.542 --> 10:34.975
Yeah, or-or maybe lunch?

10:35.043 --> 10:37.545
I had a bad experience last
time I went to the movies.

10:37.612 --> 10:39.180
We're good friends,
aren't we, Milo?

10:39.247 --> 10:41.048
We're best friends, Otis.

10:41.116 --> 10:42.416
No! No!

10:42.484 --> 10:44.285
I reject the premise of this!

10:47.556 --> 10:50.207
Okay, who's ready for
Family Movie Night?

10:50.275 --> 10:51.742
All right, tonight's selection:

10:51.810 --> 10:54.445
<i>Tim Burton's
Alice in Wonderland in 3D.</i>

10:54.513 --> 10:56.730
Now let's all sit down
and take our headache.

10:56.781 --> 10:57.731
Or...

10:57.782 --> 10:59.099
or-or...

10:59.167 --> 11:01.285
<i>we could watch...
The Cove,</i>

11:01.369 --> 11:02.503
<i>The Cove?</i>

11:02.571 --> 11:04.271
Isn't that that
horrible documentary

11:04.339 --> 11:05.472
where they kill
all the fish?

11:05.540 --> 11:07.224
Dolphins, actually.

11:07.292 --> 11:08.792
Well, yeah, but this one
was in the video store

11:08.860 --> 11:10.127
under "Ethan's Picks."

11:10.195 --> 11:11.328
Come on, Peter.

11:11.396 --> 11:12.997
Billy's our guest.

11:13.064 --> 11:14.832
<i>(sighs) All right,
we'll watch The Cove.</i>

11:16.735 --> 11:18.235
(men shouting in Japanese,
splashing and thumping)

11:18.303 --> 11:19.203
Oh, my God!

11:19.271 --> 11:20.287
I don't want to see this!

11:20.355 --> 11:21.639
I know you can't tell this,

11:21.723 --> 11:22.990
but the one who's about
to get her throat cut,

11:23.058 --> 11:25.276
she's sorta hot.

11:28.530 --> 11:31.148
Wh-Wh-What are you doing?

11:31.216 --> 11:33.083
What do you think I'm doing?
You're stoolin'?

11:33.151 --> 11:34.685
What, you gotta
do that in here?

11:34.753 --> 11:36.754
Well, where else am I
supposed to do it?

11:36.821 --> 11:39.039
I can't just do it
on the floor, can I?

11:39.107 --> 11:41.119
You'd be all, like,
"Ooh, who left this coil

11:41.144 --> 11:42.544
of rope on the floor?"

11:42.611 --> 11:44.578
It's very... comes out
very ropey is my point.

11:44.646 --> 11:46.580
But I gotta take a bath.
Go on, then.

11:46.648 --> 11:47.681
We're both men.

11:47.749 --> 11:50.284
Well... all right,
I guess.

11:50.335 --> 11:51.685
There you go!

11:51.753 --> 11:54.021
(hearty laugh)
Look at that!

11:54.089 --> 11:55.189
What is...

11:55.257 --> 11:56.790
Whoa! Solar eclipse.

11:56.858 --> 11:58.025
Blocking the sun.

11:58.093 --> 12:00.527
Do not look directly
at it. (laughs)

12:00.595 --> 12:01.628
Wh-Wha-What the hell?

12:01.680 --> 12:02.746
What're you doin'?

12:02.814 --> 12:04.014
I'm just making
a comment.

12:04.082 --> 12:05.900
Um, need to
know somethin'.

12:05.967 --> 12:08.602
Do you hear the word
"morbidly" a lot?

12:08.670 --> 12:10.337
This is not fair.
O-O-Okay.

12:10.405 --> 12:11.638
And, again, I'm gonna
ask one more question,

12:11.690 --> 12:12.923
and don't take this
the wrong way,

12:12.991 --> 12:15.138
but have you actually
got a penis?

12:15.163 --> 12:16.076
Yes.

12:16.077 --> 12:17.444
Where-where is it?
Where is it?

12:17.512 --> 12:19.213
It's in there.
Are you sure?

12:19.281 --> 12:20.948
So it's like Mr.
Snuffleupagus, is it?

12:21.016 --> 12:22.482
Aw, the hell with this.

12:22.534 --> 12:24.485
Lois, get the ruler,
we're measuring again.

12:24.552 --> 12:26.787
<i>And this time, I decide
where the base is.</i>

12:29.541 --> 12:30.841
So then I'm reading
the funnies,

12:30.909 --> 12:32.910
and right before I get
to the last panel,

12:32.978 --> 12:35.012
Billy blurts out,
he goes, he goes,

12:35.080 --> 12:38.032
"You know, those firemen showed
up to get a cat out of the tree,

12:38.099 --> 12:40.134
but it turns out it's really
Marmaduke up there."

12:40.201 --> 12:41.835
It ruined the whole damn thing!

12:41.903 --> 12:45.105
<i>Peter, in Billy's defense,
the strip is called Marmaduke,</i>

12:45.173 --> 12:47.308
and Marmaduke had not yet
made an appearance.

12:47.375 --> 12:48.909
You probably should've
seen that coming.

12:48.977 --> 12:50.511
I tell ya, he was fun at first,

12:50.578 --> 12:53.230
but now I'm not sure I can take
much more of him living here.

12:53.298 --> 12:55.766
Well, Peter, you've more than
paid back your debt to him.

12:55.834 --> 12:56.967
I mean, what did he do?

12:57.035 --> 12:58.302
He-he got you a hood ornament.

12:58.370 --> 13:00.304
If you ask me,
it's time for him to go.

13:00.372 --> 13:01.438
Yeah, you're right.

13:01.506 --> 13:02.840
Plus, the sooner
we get him out of here,

13:02.907 --> 13:05.743
the sooner I can get back
to my cocaine and dollhouses.

13:05.810 --> 13:08.145
(long, loud snorting noise)

13:15.403 --> 13:16.337
(rings bell)

13:16.404 --> 13:17.972
Dinner is served.

13:18.039 --> 13:19.673
(small excited squeal)

13:19.741 --> 13:21.308
Get out!

13:22.944 --> 13:24.478
(panting)

13:24.545 --> 13:25.779
Stewie, what's going on?

13:25.847 --> 13:27.064
Aren't you supposed
to be at day care?

13:27.132 --> 13:29.550
I escaped.
What happened to your arm?

13:29.617 --> 13:31.152
I finally stood up for all of us

13:31.220 --> 13:33.088
and told Miss Emily we should
be given a proper lunch

13:33.155 --> 13:34.756
and not just what's left over
from her Baja Fresh.

13:34.824 --> 13:36.741
And she said
I shouldn't raise my voice

13:36.809 --> 13:38.727
and pulled me really hard
into the other room,

13:38.794 --> 13:40.662
and my arm came
out of its socket.

13:40.730 --> 13:42.063
Are you sure?

13:42.131 --> 13:44.165
Are you sure you didn't
just sleep on it funny?

13:44.233 --> 13:45.950
Does this look like
I slept on it funny?!

13:46.035 --> 13:47.002
I'm gonna tell Mom!

13:47.069 --> 13:47.952
Mom!

13:48.037 --> 13:49.354
You are not going anywhere.

13:49.422 --> 13:51.506
I finally have a date
with Miss Emily tomorrow,

13:51.574 --> 13:53.308
and I'm not gonna let you
or anybody else get in my way

13:53.376 --> 13:55.276
until I have seen
every inch of her naked.

13:55.344 --> 13:56.644
Do you even hear yourself?!

13:56.712 --> 13:58.413
And what am I supposed
to do about my arm?!

13:58.464 --> 13:59.581
I'll just pop it back in.

13:59.648 --> 14:00.965
You most certainly will not!

14:01.033 --> 14:02.567
I need to go to a hospital.

14:02.635 --> 14:04.436
LOIS: Brian, is Stewie
in there with you?

14:04.520 --> 14:05.787
Mom!

14:05.855 --> 14:07.622
We're in here, Lois.
He's napping.

14:07.690 --> 14:09.757
Relax. I'm gonna
pop it back in.

14:09.809 --> 14:11.643
(muffled grunting)

14:14.914 --> 14:17.482
Get in there! C-Come on!
Hold still, Stewie!

14:17.566 --> 14:18.683
(both grunting)

14:18.751 --> 14:20.652
(shoulder popping)

14:20.736 --> 14:23.071
(coughing)

14:23.139 --> 14:25.206
I'm not saying
I like pain.

14:25.274 --> 14:27.542
But I'm not saying
I don't like it either.

14:30.846 --> 14:34.716
Hey, uh, listen, Billy, it's
been fun having you stay here,

14:34.784 --> 14:37.652
but we really need to talk about
making some new arrangements.

14:37.720 --> 14:38.853
Oh, do we?

14:38.921 --> 14:40.655
Is this because there's
some kind of problem

14:40.723 --> 14:41.689
with the hood ornament?

14:41.757 --> 14:42.690
No, that's... it's...

14:42.758 --> 14:44.376
that's... it's-it's fine.

14:44.443 --> 14:46.010
Oh, good, good.
That's good to hear,

14:46.078 --> 14:48.430
'cause it dawned on me
that the only thing better than

14:48.497 --> 14:51.149
you having one of them would
be you having two of them.

14:51.217 --> 14:53.118
Don't you say those things.

14:53.185 --> 14:54.886
Don't you say those things
unless they're true.

14:54.954 --> 14:56.354
Yeah, be quite a thing

14:56.422 --> 14:57.989
for you to have two of them,
wouldn't it?

14:58.057 --> 14:59.257
Would it ever!

15:03.446 --> 15:04.329
Wonderful!

15:04.413 --> 15:05.363
The best!

15:05.448 --> 15:06.581
Very fancy!

15:08.951 --> 15:12.320
Now, what was it you wanted
to talk to me about?

15:12.388 --> 15:13.321
Nothing, nothing.

15:13.389 --> 15:14.222
(knocking)

15:16.425 --> 15:17.358
Tricia Takanawa?

15:17.426 --> 15:18.676
What are you doing here?

15:18.744 --> 15:21.646
Peter, I'm standing here
on your front porch,

15:21.714 --> 15:24.749
hoping to kill that dolphin
with this harpoon.

15:24.817 --> 15:29.421
MAN (singing):

15:35.274 --> 15:37.909
So the thing about dolphin
lullabies is that they're all

15:37.976 --> 15:40.111
in the key of
"eee-eee"!

15:40.179 --> 15:41.813
(laughing)

15:41.880 --> 15:42.980
"Eee"!

15:43.048 --> 15:44.749
(laughing)

15:44.817 --> 15:45.950
That's loud.

15:46.018 --> 15:47.251
I get why
that's factual.

15:47.319 --> 15:48.453
I don't see
why it's funny.

15:49.738 --> 15:51.839
(laughing)
Eh-eh! What the hell, man?!

15:51.907 --> 15:53.808
Drink beer much?
(laughs)

15:53.876 --> 15:56.611
I just learned that
"much" thing from the telly.

15:56.678 --> 15:57.712
Hey, here's a question:

15:57.780 --> 15:59.514
When are you going
back to the ocean?

15:59.581 --> 16:01.933
Yeah, I mean, don't you have
family back there?

16:02.000 --> 16:04.168
I used to, but not anymore.

16:04.236 --> 16:06.404
Um, the wife won't
have me back.

16:06.472 --> 16:07.738
Threw me out, actually.

16:07.806 --> 16:09.423
Well, maybe you
should talk to her.

16:09.491 --> 16:12.426
Peter, believe me, if she'd take
me back, I'd go in a second.

16:12.494 --> 16:16.130
But she won't, so as much
as I love her, moot point.

16:16.198 --> 16:17.532
Moving on.

16:17.599 --> 16:19.300
Uh... (clears throat)

16:19.368 --> 16:21.936
Well, gotta go
and drain the eel.

16:22.004 --> 16:23.004
It's electric.

16:23.071 --> 16:25.105
(laughing):
My penis.

16:26.291 --> 16:28.392
BILLY:
Hey, throw darts much?

16:28.460 --> 16:30.195
(laughing)

16:30.263 --> 16:31.430
Boy, I see what
you're saying, Peter.

16:31.498 --> 16:32.564
Billy's annoying.

16:32.632 --> 16:34.049
Yeah, and P.S.,

16:34.117 --> 16:36.351
that guy doesn't throw
darts much. He's new.

16:39.823 --> 16:43.158
Peter, I thought you said you
were gonna ask Billy to leave.

16:43.226 --> 16:45.027
He's still sleeping
on the couch out there.

16:45.094 --> 16:46.395
I know, Lois, but I found out

16:46.462 --> 16:48.163
he's only here
'cause his wife kicked him out.

16:48.231 --> 16:51.683
So I figured out a way to kill
two birds with one stone.

16:51.768 --> 16:53.519
(chirping)
Like this.

16:53.603 --> 16:56.188
The key to that, Lois,
is big rock, small birds.

16:56.256 --> 16:57.789
Oh, and I also figured out

16:57.857 --> 17:00.058
how to achieve two goals
with one action.

17:00.126 --> 17:02.494
See, I'm gonna help Billy
get back together with his wife,

17:02.562 --> 17:04.496
and then he'll move out
and stop annoying us.

17:04.564 --> 17:05.797
How do you plan to do that?

17:05.865 --> 17:07.132
Are you kidding?

17:07.200 --> 17:08.333
I'm great at getting
people back together.

17:08.401 --> 17:10.102
I even recorded a song about it.

17:10.170 --> 17:12.304
("Reunited" intro playing)

17:12.372 --> 17:18.377
♪ Reunited
and it feels so good ♪

17:18.461 --> 17:23.765
♪ Doin' someone
that you used to do ♪

17:23.833 --> 17:26.718
♪ That's what
this song's about ♪

17:26.803 --> 17:29.938
♪ You could find someone else

17:30.006 --> 17:32.975
♪ But this
seems a little easier ♪

17:33.026 --> 17:35.944
♪ 'Cause you
already have their number ♪

17:36.012 --> 17:37.312
♪ Yeah, yeah...

17:40.783 --> 17:41.984
Hey, guys.

17:42.051 --> 17:44.486
Everybody having
fun playing with...

17:44.554 --> 17:46.038
What-what is that?

17:46.122 --> 17:49.057
A piece of wood with a,
with a nail in it. Neat.

17:49.125 --> 17:50.259
He can't hear you.

17:50.326 --> 17:51.627
There was a kitchen
explosion today,

17:51.694 --> 17:53.161
and half the kids are deaf.

17:53.229 --> 17:55.013
Oh, hi, Brian.
Hey, Emily.

17:55.081 --> 17:56.148
Wow, you look great.

17:56.216 --> 17:57.316
You're ready to go?

17:57.383 --> 17:58.350
Yeah, one sec.

17:58.418 --> 17:59.585
I'm leaving, honey.

17:59.652 --> 18:01.253
Okay, babe, have fun.

18:01.321 --> 18:04.022
I'm probably just gonna take
a couple more showers.

18:04.090 --> 18:05.324
Who-who was that?

18:05.391 --> 18:06.658
That's my boyfriend, Devin.

18:06.726 --> 18:07.759
Are you ready for lunch?

18:10.146 --> 18:12.648
RADIO DISPATCHER: 11-25,
Code 6, 105 North Avenue...

18:12.715 --> 18:14.215
What you did
to these kids...

18:14.267 --> 18:17.486
There is a special place
in hell for people like you.

18:21.140 --> 18:23.609
Come on, let's go home.

18:23.676 --> 18:25.444
Man, when she
gets to jail,

18:25.511 --> 18:27.279
she's gonna be
major lez-chow.

18:27.347 --> 18:30.449
She sure is, Stewie.
She sure is.

18:33.703 --> 18:35.904
I'm telling you, Peter,
you're wasting your time.

18:35.955 --> 18:37.456
She's never taking me back.

18:37.540 --> 18:39.091
Well, you'll never
know until you try.

18:39.175 --> 18:41.677
Hey, I brought this sack
of garbage from my home.

18:41.744 --> 18:43.244
Where do I put this?
Just anywhere?

18:43.296 --> 18:44.630
Yeah. Anywhere.

18:46.966 --> 18:49.017
Yay, people!

18:49.085 --> 18:50.269
All right, here she comes.

18:50.353 --> 18:52.437
Oh, hello, Joanne.

18:52.522 --> 18:53.972
Billy?! What are
you doing here?

18:54.057 --> 18:57.609
He's here because he loves you,
and he wants to patch things up.

18:57.694 --> 18:59.427
Hey, how come
you ain't got boobs?

18:59.479 --> 19:01.063
You like a runner
or something?

19:01.114 --> 19:02.230
Who's this, then?

19:02.282 --> 19:03.949
He's just a friend,
trying to help.

19:04.033 --> 19:06.101
Look, Billy,
I don't care

19:06.152 --> 19:09.771
what you or your fat friend
here has to say, it's over.

19:09.822 --> 19:12.791
(sighs) Well, thanks
for trying.

19:12.875 --> 19:14.660
I knew she wouldn't
listen to you, though.

19:14.744 --> 19:16.628
Well, maybe so.

19:16.713 --> 19:19.715
<i>But I know someone
she'll have to listen to.</i>

19:19.782 --> 19:21.249
Hey, gang,
I'm Aquaman.

19:21.301 --> 19:22.884
Get back together.

19:22.952 --> 19:24.720
Boop-boop-boop-boop-
boop-boop-boop.

19:24.787 --> 19:26.588
That's not
Aquaman!

19:26.639 --> 19:28.090
Billy, what
is going on?

19:28.141 --> 19:29.341
Let me answer that.

19:29.425 --> 19:32.145
Look, Joanne, Billy had
nothing to do with this.

19:32.229 --> 19:35.315
It was just a dumb plan my
buddies and I put together

19:35.399 --> 19:37.466
because we know how
much Billy loves you.

19:37.518 --> 19:39.435
And he misses you very much.

19:39.486 --> 19:41.487
Look, just give him
another chance.

19:41.572 --> 19:44.857
And if you won't do it
for me, do it for Fish Jesus.

19:44.942 --> 19:46.909
Do you have Fish Jesus?
Of course.

19:46.977 --> 19:49.645
He was nailed to a board
and hung in a man's study

19:49.697 --> 19:52.115
as a novelty to
sing funny songs.

19:52.166 --> 19:54.334
Your god is a gag gift,
did you know that?

19:54.418 --> 19:55.668
Would you excuse us?

19:56.954 --> 19:59.155
Is it true, Billy?

19:59.206 --> 20:00.506
Do you really miss me?

20:00.591 --> 20:02.342
Joanne, I am so sorry.

20:02.426 --> 20:03.876
I promise
I'll do better.

20:03.961 --> 20:05.878
You know what?
I had to live on the land

20:05.963 --> 20:08.181
to learn there might
be a million fish in the sea,

20:08.265 --> 20:10.216
but there's only one you.

20:10.300 --> 20:12.085
Oh, Billy...

20:17.507 --> 20:19.175
Aw, look at that.

20:19.226 --> 20:21.361
That's nice.

20:21.445 --> 20:24.097
Oh, cool, they're
already using my garbage!

20:29.486 --> 20:31.487
Hey, Brian, thanks for helping
get rid of Miss Emily.

20:31.555 --> 20:32.722
Although I've got to say,

20:32.790 --> 20:34.724
my new preschool teacher
is even hotter.

20:34.792 --> 20:35.892
Really?
Yeah.

20:35.959 --> 20:37.126
Let me know if you
want his number.

20:37.194 --> 20:39.796
Oh, you!

20:39.863 --> 20:41.230
Okay, now just
stay like this

20:41.298 --> 20:43.216
and let Peter and Lois
finish their thing.

20:43.283 --> 20:45.385
Wow, Peter, you did
a really nice thing

20:45.452 --> 20:47.820
helping Billy get back
together with his wife.

20:47.888 --> 20:49.279
Yeah, and the best part
is, he's out of the house

20:49.304 --> 20:50.504
and back in the ocean.

20:50.591 --> 20:52.575
I guess everything
worked out for everybody.

20:54.878 --> 20:57.880
Arr! 'Tis a mighty haul!

20:57.931 --> 20:59.432
Hey.
Oh.

20:59.500 --> 21:01.501
Yeah, it's me as Neptune.

21:01.502 --> 22:02.502
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru